{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS3ANw33BHbvYoMAGn4j","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The job has failed every night, and the script had a bug that stopped it from telling you. I fixed the bug, but the underlying login problem still needs your credentials. I haven't run the job under launchd, so none of this is tested end to end.\n\n1. **Script bug (fixed):** `bin/nightly-review.zsh` did `status=$?`, and `status` is a read-only variable in zsh. Every run died at line 19 with `read-only variable: status`, before it reached the call that sends the failure note. I renamed the variable to `rc`, and `zsh -n` accepts the script.\n2. **Login failure (not fixed):** `claude -p` logs `Not logged in · Please run /login` on every run. The launchd job can't use the login from your terminal session. It needs a non-interactive credential, such as a token from `claude setup-token` exposed as `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN`, or `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`. I didn't add one because it needs your secret.\n\nUntil you add that credential, you'll get a \"nightly review FAILED\" Telegram message each night, which is the intended behaviour.\n\nI also couldn't test whether `notify.sh` can read the bot token from the keychain under launchd. If the failure notes still don't arrive, check `Library/Logs/nightly-review.err` first.\n\nThe causes and these caveats are written up in `ANSWER.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":357,"cache_read_input_tokens":25097,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":357},"output_tokens":460,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d86aac20-5739-4e95-aa9f-6e05a50dd32f","uuid":"ced61571-52fc-400b-b828-94675b4f5168","timest